This directory's verifier logic ports constraint-type semantics from IFEval
(the Instruction-Following Eval), Copyright The Google Research Authors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The source it was ported from is
vendored in this repo at data/verih/Eval/evals/ifeval/utils/instructions.py.

Ported into coverage_pool.py / precision_pool.py (IFEval instruction id → our
verifier type):
  change_case:english_capital / english_lowercase   -> casing
  punctuation:no_comma                              -> no_commas
  detectable_format:title                           -> title
  startend:end_checker                              -> end_phrase
  keywords:frequency                                -> keyword_frequency
  length_constraints:number_paragraphs              -> paragraph_count
  change_case:capital_word_frequency                -> caps_word_frequency
plus the semantics of keywords:existence/forbidden_words, detectable_content:
number_placeholders, detectable_format:multiple_sections, and length_constraints:
number_words/number_sentences (our keyword_include/exclude, no_placeholders,
required_sections, word_count/sentence_count).

Deliberate deviations from IFEval, to keep the on-pod GRPO reward path
dependency-free (no nltk / langdetect):
  1. the casing checks drop IFEval's langdetect "response is English" clause
     (our composed prompts are English by construction);
  2. caps_word_frequency uses a regex word tokenizer, not nltk.word_tokenize.

NOT from IFEval — original checks for the E08 execution_slip / coverage failure
modes: arithmetic_result (embedded computation whose result must appear) and
ordering (items must appear in a required order).
